A Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) is a logically isolated section of the cloud that you can control and customize. It allows you to define your own network space, configure network components like subnets, route tables, and gateways, and control how your instances communicate with each other and the internet.

In a multi-tenant SaaS deployment, a VPC can be used to provide a secure and isolated environment for each tenant. This helps to prevent data leakage between tenants and provides a level of security and privacy.

