A VPC is a logically isolated section of the cloud that you can control and customize. Here's a simple example of how you might define a VPC using Terraform:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "my_vpc" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
  tags = {
    Name = "my_vpc"
  }
}
```

This Terraform code will create a new VPC in the AWS us-west-2 region with a CIDR block of 10.0.0.0/16 and a tag of "my_vpc". 

Please note that this is a very basic example and a real-world VPC configuration would be much more complex, including subnets, route tables, internet gateways, security groups, etc.

